  "tldr": "The fixed \\(r=2\\) Conflict Graph Design estimator is proposed to obey a sharp uniform normal-inference frontier: under bounded empirical endpoint fourth moments and the published non-superefficiency scale, Gaussian approximation holds for every graph class with \\(d_n=o(n^{2/3})\\), and it fails uniformly whenever this condition is violated. The sufficient direction uses the exact forward Doob martingale in the design's independent desired-exposure coordinates and a prefix-sensitive quadratic-variation bound; the necessary direction uses repeated Perron-ordered stars whose standardized estimator converges to an explicit nonnormal Gaussian--Poisson law at the boundary. The same argument yields uniform ratio consistency for the published spectral variance-bound estimator and uniformly conservative feasible Wald coverage throughout the normal regime.",
